quran[10]{c,v,t}:
  21,1,"The (time of) reckoning for the people has drawn closer, yet they are turning away heedlessly."
  21,2,"Whatever new Reminder comes to them from their Lord, they only listen to it playfully,"
  21,3,with their hearts (totally) distracted. Those who are unjust secretly whisper: ‘Is not this (man) just a human being like yourselves? Will you surrender to (his) magic while you see clearly?’
  21,4,"He said: ‘My Lord knows every word (spoken) in the heaven and the earth. And He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.’"
  21,5,"Yet they said: ‘(These Reminders are) confused dreams! Rather, he has fabricated it! Rather, he is a poet! Let him bring us a sign like the former (messengers) were sent (with signs).’"
  21,6,Not a (single) town We destroyed before them ever believed (after receiving the signs). Will these (pagans) then now believe?
  21,7,"We did not send (the messengers) before you, except men to whom We revealed. So ask the People of the Reminder if you do not know."
  21,8,"And We did not make them bodies (of such nature) that would not eat food, nor were they to abide forever."
  21,9,"Then We fulfilled the promise to them. So We delivered them and whomever We willed, and We destroyed the transgressors."
  21,10,"Indeed, We have (now) revealed to you a Book in which there is your Reminder. Will you still not understand?"
